  "semantic_review": {
    "coverage": "All 36 paired raw/segment outputs independently reviewed; model review, not human certification.",
    "english_gain": "EN011 -24 dB pause-after loses unsupported trailing words and becomes a strict pass; pause-before recovers the sentence but adds two unsupported sound labels.",
    "japanese_loss": "JA010 -42 dB pause-before loses its strict pass by repeating the complete sentence. -24 dB pause-after goes from two copies to three. Count three and negation remain; these are repetitions, not negation loss.",
    "mandarin_name": "ZH034 original changes 辛格 to 新格 and loses the frozen spelling/name anchor. Both arms already misrecognize the song word; this is not proof of a different person.",
    "unchanged_semantic_limits": "JA025 substitutes 適用 for 適応; ZH001 substitutes 克隆 for 科隆. Passing the frozen error threshold does not prove perfect meaning.",
    "anchor_label_limits": "Mandarin -42 dB outputs retain 无法. The negation-labelled anchor requires the entire exact phrase 无法长途跋涉, so lexical corruption also fails it; no polarity reversal demonstrated."
  },
  "control_scope": "Six language labels reuse two WAVs. Strict empty requires no text AND no segments, not punctuation-normalized scoring. All six outputs are identical between arms and fail. Exact-zero WAV bytes are unchanged. Standard CLI omits production exact-zero bypass; these silence hallucinations establish no JNI/Kotlin zero-guard bug.",
